DESCRIPTION:November 11 is Origami Day in Japan\, a date the Nippon Origami
  Association settled on in 1980\, and it is also the closing day of World 
 Origami Days\, the folding season OrigamiUSA runs from October 24. The dat
 e was chosen for its arithmetic: written 11/11\, it is four ones\, read as
  the four sides of a square sheet of paper.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com
 /holiday/world-origami-day/
